FIGURES
Do not reproduce, adapt, trace, or closely imitate any published figure.
For every proposed figure provide:
1.	Figure number.
2.	Descriptive title.
3.	Original figure brief.
4.	Panel layout.
5.	Labels.
6.	Arrows and relationships.
7.	Suggested colour coding.
8.	Single principal teaching point.
9.	Relevant source citations.
The figure brief must allow a medical illustrator to create an original conceptual figure without reconstructing an existing published image.
If a figure summarizes published data, cite the underlying data sources.
